--
N5008 [dcl.fct]/6-7: `using PMF = int (S::*)(int) const;` -- the cv-qualifier-seq
of a function declarator in a type-id belongs to the function type (it
qualifies the implicit object parameter).  The parser merged it into the
declared type as if it were a cv-qualifier of `int`, so the alias spelling
denoted a pointer-to-member of const int with the return type lost, while the
typedef spelling (which keeps its declarator) was fine.  Pointer-to-DATA-member
access `s.*pmd` is a separate, still open gap.
